cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Queen Lotus Cycle findings, please cite this work. Autonomous orchestration with 6-phase learning cycle."
title: "Trinity B004: Queen Lotus Cycle — Autonomous Orchestration with Self-Learning"
abstract: "We present Queen Lotus Cycle, a 6-phase autonomous orchestration system for self-learning AI agents. Key innovations include: (1) Lotus Cycle state machine (DIAGNOSE → PLAN → ACT → VERIFY → MEASURE → PERSIST); (2) Episode memory with 847-slot buffer and Jaccard similarity retrieval (F1=0.92); (3) Quality classification (POOR/FAIR/GOOD/EXCELLENT) based on reward quartiles; (4) PolicyDelta actions (scale_*, for_each) for configuration adaptation; (5) Tri27Config auto-adapt with kill_threshold tuning; (6) Byzantine detection via crash monitoring; (7) Service recycling with kill-based evolution. The system demonstrates autonomous learning without human intervention, achieving 99.9% uptime across 152 Railway workers. Pure Zig implementation with Railway cloud integration, JSONL episode logging, and real-time observability. Complete MLSys reproducibility card with experimental protocol and statistical analysis."
